   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 08 — Temporal Validation & Walk-Forward Cross-Validation\n",
    "\n",
    "**Motivation (professor feedback):**  \n",
    "> *"The dataset and temporal methodology also need further refinement before the reported probabilities can be treated as production-grade."*\n",
    "\n",
    "The original evaluation used a **single temporal split** at block 17,000,000 (≈ April 2023),\n",
    "producing only **205 test wallets** — too small for reliable AUC estimation (high variance).\n",
    "This notebook replaces that single point estimate with:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Walk-forward cross-validation**: train on periods 1..k, test on period k+1, iterate across 6 folds — gives mean AUC ± std across time windows.\n",
    "2. **Out-of-time validation**: train exclusively on 2021–2022 data, test on 2023 — the strictest form of temporal holdout.\n",
    "3. **AUC stability analysis**: confirms the model degrades gracefully over time, not catastrophically.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why this matters:**  \n",
    "In production credit models, AUC variance across time windows is as important as average AUC.\n",
    "A model with AUC 0.68 ± 0.02 is operationally safer than one with 0.71 ± 0.12."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys\n",
    "sys.path.insert(0, '..')\n",
    "\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import matplotlib.ticker as mtick\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "\n",
    "from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\n",
    "from sklearn.calibration import CalibratedClassifierCV\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import roc_auc_score, brier_score_loss\n",
    "import lightgbm as lgb\n",
    "\n",
    "sns.set_theme(style='whitegrid', context='notebook', palette='muted')\n",
    "BLUE   = '#185FA5'\n",
    "ORANGE = '#E07B39'\n",
    "GREEN  = '#2E9E6B'\n",
    "GREY   = '#8A9BB4'\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Libraries loaded.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Load data and map blocks to approximate dates\n",
    "\n",
    "Ethereum block → approximate date conversion:\n",
    "- **Pre-merge** (before block ≈15,537,393, September 15 2022): ~13 seconds/block\n",
    "- **Post-merge** (after block ≈15,537,393): ~12 seconds/block\n",
    "\n",
    "We use the Genesis anchor (block 0 = July 30, 2015) and a piecewise linear approximation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df = pd.read_parquet('../data/processed/feature_matrix.parquet')\n",
    "\n",
    "NON_FEATURE_COLS = {'wallet', 'label', 'first_tx_block', 'last_tx_block'}\n",
    "feature_cols = [c for c in df.columns if c not in NON_FEATURE_COLS]\n",
    "\n",
    "MERGE_BLOCK = 15_537_393  # Sep 15, 2022\n",
    "MERGE_TS    = pd.Timestamp('2022-09-15')\n",
    "GENESIS_TS  = pd.Timestamp('2015-07-30')\n",
    "\n",
    "def block_to_date(block: pd.Series) -> pd.Series:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Piecewise linear block → date approximation.\"\"\"\n",
    "    pre_mask  = block <= MERGE_BLOCK\n",
    "    pre_secs  = (block - 0) * 13\n",
    "    post_secs = (MERGE_BLOCK * 13) + (block - MERGE_BLOCK) * 12\n",
    "    secs = np.where(pre_mask, pre_secs, post_secs)\n",
    "    return GENESIS_TS + pd.to_timedelta(secs, unit='s')\n",
    "\n",
    "df['first_tx_date'] = block_to_date(df['first_tx_block'])\n",
    "df['quarter']       = df['first_tx_date'].dt.to_period('Q')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Feature matrix: {df.shape[0]:,} wallets, {len(feature_cols)} features')\n",
    "print(f'First wallet active: {df[\"first_tx_date\"].min().date()}')\n",
    "print(f'Last  wallet active: {df[\"first_tx_date\"].max().date()}')\n",
    "print(f'\\nWallets per quarter (first active):')\n",
    "print(df['quarter'].value_counts().sort_index().to_string())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Problem with single split: illustrating the variance issue"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.utils import resample\n",
    "\n",
    "SPLIT_BLOCK = 17_000_000\n",
    "train_mask  = df['first_tx_block'] <= SPLIT_BLOCK\n",
    "test_mask   = ~train_mask\n",
    "\n",
    "X_tr = df.loc[train_mask, feature_cols]\n",
    "y_tr = df.loc[train_mask, 'label']\n",
    "X_te = df.loc[test_mask,  feature_cols]\n",
    "y_te = df.loc[test_mask,  'label']\n",
    "\n",
    "pipe = Pipeline([\n",
    "    ('scaler', StandardScaler()),\n",
    "    ('clf',    LogisticRegression(C=0.1, class_weight='balanced', max_iter=1000, random_state=42)),\n",
    "])\n",
    "pipe.fit(X_tr, y_tr)\n",
    "prob_te = pipe.predict_proba(X_te)[:, 1]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Bootstrap confidence interval on the 205-wallet test set\n",
    "n_boot = 2000\n",
    "boot_aucs = []\n",
    "rng = np.random.default_rng(42)\n",
    "for _ in range(n_boot):\n",
    "    idx = rng.integers(0, len(y_te), len(y_te))\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        boot_aucs.append(roc_auc_score(y_te.values[idx], prob_te[idx]))\n",
    "    except Exception:\n",
    "        pass\n",
    "\n",
    "auc_point  = roc_auc_score(y_te, prob_te)\n",
    "auc_lo, auc_hi = np.percentile(boot_aucs, [2.5, 97.5])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Single-split test set: {len(y_te)} wallets')\n",
    "print(f'ROC-AUC: {auc_point:.4f}  (95% CI: {auc_lo:.4f} – {auc_hi:.4f})')\n",
    "print(f'CI width: {auc_hi - auc_lo:.4f}  ← very wide due to small n')\n",
    "print(f'\\nTrain default rate: {y_tr.mean():.2%}')\n",
    "print(f'Test  default rate: {y_te.mean():.2%}  ← differs from train by {abs(y_tr.mean()-y_te.mean()):.2%}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Walk-forward cross-validation\n",
    "\n",
    "**Scheme:** Sort wallets by first active quarter. At each fold k (k ≥ 2):\n",
    "- **Train**: wallets first active in quarters 0..k  \n",
    "- **Test**: wallets first active in quarter k+1\n",
    "\n",
    "This mirrors production deployment: the model is trained on all historical wallets  \n",
    "and evaluated on newly-seen wallets from the next time window."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "quarters = sorted(df['quarter'].unique())\n",
    "print(f'Quarters available: {[str(q) for q in quarters]}')\n",
    "\n",
    "def make_pipeline():\n",
    "    return Pipeline([\n",
    "        ('scaler', StandardScaler()),\n",
    "        ('clf',    LogisticRegression(C=0.1, class_weight='balanced',\n",
    "                                      max_iter=1000, random_state=42)),\n",
    "    ])\n",
    "\n",
    "walk_results = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for i in range(2, len(quarters) - 1):\n",
    "    train_quarters = quarters[:i+1]\n",
    "    test_quarter   = quarters[i+1]\n",
    "\n",
    "    train_mask = df['quarter'].isin(train_quarters)\n",
    "    test_mask  = df['quarter'] == test_quarter\n",
    "\n",
    "    y_train = df.loc[train_mask, 'label']\n",
    "    y_test  = df.loc[test_mask,  'label']\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Skip if test has fewer than 2 classes or < 30 wallets\n",
    "    if test_mask.sum() < 30 or y_test.nunique() < 2:\n",
    "        print(f'Skipping fold {i+1} ({test_quarter}): only {test_mask.sum()} wallets')\n",
    "        continue\n",
    "\n",
    "    X_train = df.loc[train_mask, feature_cols]\n",
    "    X_test  = df.loc[test_mask,  feature_cols]\n",
    "\n",
    "    pipe = make_pipeline()\n",
    "    pipe.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
    "    prob = pipe.predict_proba(X_test)[:, 1]\n",
    "\n",
    "    auc    = roc_auc_score(y_test, prob)\n",
    "    brier  = brier_score_loss(y_test, prob)\n",
    "\n",
    "    walk_results.append({\n",
    "        'fold':              i + 1,\n",
    "        'test_quarter':      str(test_quarter),\n",
    "        'train_size':        train_mask.sum(),\n",
    "        'test_size':         test_mask.sum(),\n",
    "        'test_default_rate': y_test.mean(),\n",
    "        'roc_auc':           auc,\n",
    "        'brier':             brier,\n",
    "    })\n",
    "    print(f'Fold {i+1:2d} | Test quarter: {test_quarter} | n={test_mask.sum():4d} '\n",
    "          f'| default_rate={y_test.mean():.2%} | AUC={auc:.4f} | Brier={brier:.4f}')\n",
    "\n",
    "wf_df = pd.DataFrame(walk_results)\n",
    "print(f'\\n━━━ Walk-forward summary ━━━')\n",
    "print(f'Mean AUC:  {wf_df[\"roc_auc\"].mean():.4f}')\n",
    "print(f'Std  AUC:  {wf_df[\"roc_auc\"].std():.4f}')\n",
    "print(f'Min  AUC:  {wf_df[\"roc_auc\"].min():.4f}')\n",
    "print(f'Max  AUC:  {wf_df[\"roc_auc\"].max():.4f}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Out-of-time validation (2021–2022 train → 2023 test)\n",
    "\n",
    "The strictest temporal holdout: the model sees **zero data from 2023** during training.\n",
    "This simulates deploying a model trained at end-2022 and evaluating it on new wallets in 2023."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Block numbers approximate to January 1 each year\n",
    "BLOCK_JAN2021 = 11_565_019\n",
    "BLOCK_JAN2023 = 16_308_190\n",
    "\n",
    "oot_train_mask = (df['first_tx_block'] >= BLOCK_JAN2021) & (df['first_tx_block'] < BLOCK_JAN2023)\n",
    "oot_test_mask  =  df['first_tx_block'] >= BLOCK_JAN2023\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Out-of-time split:')\n",
    "print(f'  Train (2021–2022): {oot_train_mask.sum():,} wallets | '\n",
    "      f'default rate: {df.loc[oot_train_mask, \"label\"].mean():.2%}')\n",
    "print(f'  Test  (2023+):     {oot_test_mask.sum():,} wallets  | '\n",
    "      f'default rate: {df.loc[oot_test_mask, \"label\"].mean():.2%}')\n",
    "\n",
    "X_oot_train = df.loc[oot_train_mask, feature_cols]\n",
    "y_oot_train = df.loc[oot_train_mask, 'label']\n",
    "X_oot_test  = df.loc[oot_test_mask,  feature_cols]\n",
    "y_oot_test  = df.loc[oot_test_mask,  'label']\n",
    "\n",
    "# Train both models on 2021-2022\n",
    "lr_oot = make_pipeline()\n",
    "lr_oot.fit(X_oot_train, y_oot_train)\n",
    "\n",
    "n_pos = int(y_oot_train.sum())\n",
    "n_neg = len(y_oot_train) - n_pos\n",
    "lgb_base = lgb.LGBMClassifier(\n",
    "    n_estimators=300, learning_rate=0.05, num_leaves=31,\n",
    "    scale_pos_weight=n_neg/n_pos, random_state=42, verbose=-1, n_jobs=-1,\n",
    ")\n",
    "lgb_base.fit(X_oot_train, y_oot_train)\n",
    "\n",
    "lr_prob_oot  = lr_oot.predict_proba(X_oot_test)[:, 1]\n",
    "lgb_prob_oot = lgb_base.predict_proba(X_oot_test)[:, 1]\n",
    "\n",
    "lr_auc_oot   = roc_auc_score(y_oot_test, lr_prob_oot)\n",
    "lgb_auc_oot  = roc_auc_score(y_oot_test, lgb_prob_oot)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'\\nOut-of-time ROC-AUC:')\n",
    "print(f'  Logistic Regression: {lr_auc_oot:.4f}')\n",
    "print(f'  LightGBM:            {lgb_auc_oot:.4f}')\n",
    "print(f'\\nBrier score (lower is better):')\n",
    "print(f'  Logistic Regression: {brier_score_loss(y_oot_test, lr_prob_oot):.4f}')\n",
    "print(f'  LightGBM:            {brier_score_loss(y_oot_test, lgb_prob_oot):.4f}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. AUC stability plot"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b6",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 5))\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Left: Walk-forward AUC by fold ──────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "ax = axes[0]\n",
    "ax.plot(wf_df['test_quarter'], wf_df['roc_auc'], marker='o', color=BLUE, lw=2, ms=7, label='LR (walk-forward)')\n",
    "ax.axhline(wf_df['roc_auc'].mean(), color=BLUE, ls='--', alpha=0.5, label=f'Mean AUC = {wf_df[\"roc_auc\"].mean():.4f}')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Confidence band (mean ± std)\n",
    "mean_auc = wf_df['roc_auc'].mean()\n",
    "std_auc  = wf_df['roc_auc'].std()\n",
    "ax.axhspan(mean_auc - std_auc, mean_auc + std_auc, alpha=0.08, color=BLUE, label=f'±1 std ({std_auc:.4f})')\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.axhline(0.5, color='grey', ls=':', lw=1, label='Random baseline')\n",
    "ax.set_ylim(0.4, 0.85)\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel('Test quarter (wallet first active)')\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel('ROC-AUC')\n",
    "ax.set_title('Walk-forward cross-validation\\n(train on quarters 0..k, test on k+1)')\n",
    "ax.legend(fontsize=9)\n",
    "ax.tick_params(axis='x', rotation=30)\n",
    "ax.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Right: Test set size vs AUC scatter ────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "ax2 = axes[1]\n",
    "sc = ax2.scatter(wf_df['test_size'], wf_df['roc_auc'], c=range(len(wf_df)),\n",
    "                 cmap='Blues', s=80, zorder=3, edgecolors='white', linewidths=0.5)\n",
    "ax2.axhline(0.5, color='grey', ls=':', lw=1)\n",
    "ax2.set_xlabel('Test fold size (# wallets)')\n",
    "ax2.set_ylabel('ROC-AUC')\n",
    "ax2.set_title('AUC vs test fold size\\n(larger folds = more reliable estimates)')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Mark the original single-split test set\n",
    "ax2.scatter([205], [auc_point], color='red', s=120, zorder=5,\n",
    "            marker='*', label=f'Original single split (n=205, AUC={auc_point:.3f})')\n",
    "ax2.legend(fontsize=9)\n",
    "ax2.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
    "plt.colorbar(sc, ax=ax2, label='Fold index')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.suptitle('ChainScore — Temporal validation (Phase 1 rigor check)', y=1.01, fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig('../reports/figures/temporal_validation.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "print('Plot saved.')"
   ]
  },
  {
